  - q: "How does the Word & Character Counter calculate word count?"
    a: "The tool analyzes your input string and splits words using whitespace boundaries. Hyphenated words and special characters are evaluated according to standard English linguistic rules to provide accurate real-time metrics."
  - q: "What is the difference between characters with and without spaces?"
    a: "Characters with spaces count every single keypress including letters, numbers, punctuation, and whitespace gaps. Characters without spaces exclude blank space gaps, measuring strictly visible printed characters."
  - q: "How is the estimated reading time calculated?"
    a: "Estimated reading time is calculated using an average adult reading speed benchmark of 200 words per minute. Estimated speaking time uses an average oral presentation speed of 130 words per minute."
  - q: "Why are common stop words excluded from top used words?"
    a: "Common English words like 'the', 'is', and 'and' occur frequently in every sentence. Filtering out stop words highlights meaningful keywords and main topic density in your text."
  - q: "Is my typed text saved or transmitted to a server?"
